 but the 14k's 23 J5 and 27 F5 gave it back. After White's 28 H6 the game settled at about 6 points for White and stayed there to the end.", "moments": [{"turn": 6, "text": "Opus 5.5 played C6 with Black ahead by 6.8 in White's favour, wait: the lead was -6.8, so White was ahead, and the move lost 8.8 points, swinging the lead to +2.0 for Black. The engine preferred E4, next to Black's lone stone at E5."}, {"turn": 7, "text": "The 14k handed the points straight back with G3, losing 9.1 and turning +2.0 into -7.1. The engine wanted E4, the point Black would take two turns later."}, {"turn": 10, "text": "D5 was the worst move of the game for Opus 5.5, losing 10.9 points and turning -0.2 into +10.6 for Black. White had been level, and the engine preferred E7."}, {"turn": 11, "text": "The 14k answered with G6, which lost 6.4 and brought the lead back from +10.6 to +4.2. The engine's choice was E7, the point Opus 5.5 only took at turn 18."}, {"turn": 23, "text": "J5 cost the 14k 8.2 points and moved the lead from +2.2 to -6.0. The engine wanted H6, the point White later claimed."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "Opus 5.5 played G5 and lost 8.3 points, sending the lead from -6.0 back to +2.4 for Black. The engine's choice was H6, and the 14k answered with F5, which lost 8.1 and swung it back."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "H6 was the engine's own choice and lost nothing, holding the lead at -5.8 for White. From here the lead stayed near -6 through the endgame, and the final stretch of fills at A7, A8, E9 and G9 gave away almost nothing."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and report groups, liberties and area counts for the current position, with no candidate loops or lookahead. The other commands append to games.md and CLAUDE.md as notes, and the denied sed was just a notes edit.", "stop": false}}